*****************
** MANIFEST
*****************

The EHS repo is maintained at url = ssh://inx-data@server/home/inx-data/data/Repos/EHS.git
This build system for EHS requires linux (debian usually) and the following repos to be cecked out in to the same directory:

EHS                (Contains this readme file)
EHS-build-support  (Contains toolchains and Basic OS dependencies)
comp-lib-support   (Contains optional pre-built components for each suport platform)

It is advisable to also check out the following repos to build production installs:
apps               (Contains applications which maybe installed into production packages)

The following repositories are required for building and deploying inxware tools and services:
dist               (Desktop tool environment strucuture)
tools              (Desktop tools source code)
BrixBuild          (Build system to create the BRIX product variant of inxware - packages referenced on the Brix web site)
DevmanServer  
brix               (OpenGL development version of tools  )

All the above repos are available at ssh://inx-data@server/home/inx-data/data/Repos/*.git

*****************
** BUILDING eRT Locally
*****************

The command steps needed to build EHS for a specific target:

make help 

to get a list of supported targets type
./configure help

************************
** Specific Pltform Notes
*************************
e.g.
./configure linux_x86_gtk_gst
make prepdeps
make all
make targetenv HOST_OS_CONFIG_SCRIPTS_EXTRA="0140-update-kernel-4-8-16-debian"
make targetenv_version
make targetenv_deb UPLOAD=ambifier@www.ambifier.com/home/ambifier/deb-repo
